# A Raspberry Pi 5 with 8 GB on Raspberry Pi OS Lite, 64-bit: Debian bookworm on arm64, no screen, no keyring.
DESCRIPTION="Raspberry Pi 5, 8 GB, Raspberry Pi OS Lite (Debian bookworm, arm64)"
PLATFORM=linux/arm64
BASE=debian:bookworm
CPUS=4
MEMORY_MB=8192
# Its four Cortex-A76 cores do about as much as two cores of a recent Mac (run.sh --speed; a rough idea only).
SPEED_CPUS=2.2
# The apt packages it gets, from deploy/: the list install-pi.sh installs on the real one.
PACKAGES=pi-packages.txt
# The user TARS runs as there; the clone is at ~/voice-assistant, as install-pi.sh has it.
USER_NAME=pi
